From e32dd607b55b9c6afd605482a4bc31c9d30528d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:45:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Make the local verifier the state authority of
 independent CLI and MCP reads

With --chain-verifier (CLI) / chainVerifier (MCP profile, hosted-connector registry,
host-lifecycle plan), independent mode's chain is cli/independent.mjs VerifiedChain via one
factory, independentChain: the QuorumChain interface over network/verified-chain.mjs (one
confirmed, fresh, monotonic block per snapshot, whole-operation deadline, terminal client).

- snapshot/read/readMany/balance and quorumPublicClient (the SDK view) read the verifier; an
  eth_call revert from the verifier is a fact (agreed revert), anything else an outage.
- sendQuorumTx simulates at the verified block (an opt-in proof-backed `call` on the pinned
  client); nonce, gas, fees, broadcast and receipts use only the explicit --rpc transport
  (all configured endpoints must agree), and the verifier must reach the receipt's block
  before a send returns (else the outcome is unknown). Without a transport every
  transaction/history method refuses by name. Log scans inside a snapshot are discovery
  hints from that transport only, clamped to the verified block.
- the --rpc list is optional under the verifier and never falls back to the public default
  list; custody's own quorum reader (leaseReaderClients) refuses instead of reading the
  transport.
- MCP Scope reads each tool call at ONE verified block; resumed reads use a floor-free
  snapshot that still requires the exact hash to be canonical and fresh, so concurrent calls
  do not refuse each other. The signer's receipt and nonce look-ups use historySnapshot.

The legacy RPC quorum is unchanged when no verifier is chosen.
